>> title: Turkey Pan Gravy
>> category: Sauces & Gravies
>> tags: turkey, roux, thanksgiving, stovetop
>> counters: Diner, Meat and Three
>> aka: turkey gravy, giblet gravy, pan gravy
>> servings: 8
>> time: 25 min
>> slack: narrow — the stock goes in a ladle at a time against a whisk, or it lumps for good and no straining hides it

>> step: cook roux 3 min
Cook @all-purpose flour{1/3%cup}(40 g) in @turkey pan drippings{1/3%cup}(80 mL; the skimmed fat) in a #saucepan{} over medium heat for ~{3%min}, whisking to a nut-brown roux.

>> step: deglaze, reduce by half
Deglaze the #roasting pan{} with @dry white wine{1/2%cup}(120 mL), scraping up every brown bit, and reduce by half.

>> step: whisk in a ladle at a time
Whisk @turkey stock{3%cups}(700 mL; warm, plus the defatted pan juices) into @&(~2)roux{} a ladle at a time.

>> step: simmer 10 min
Simmer @&(~2)pan reduction{} with @&(~1)gravy base{}, @thyme{2%sprigs}, and @bay leaf{1} for ~{10%min}.

>> step: season
Season @&(~1)gravy{} with @kosher salt{1/2%tsp} and @black pepper{1/2%tsp}, then strain.
